<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb copper cable shipments, orders fall.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb copper cable shipments, orders fall.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese copper wire and cable shipments and orders fell in February from the same month last year, the Japanese Electric Wire and Cable Makers' Association said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Shipments registered their first year-on-year decline in six months, the association said.</p>
<p>The automobile and construction sectors continued to show strong demand growth, while exports were boosted by the weakness of the yen against the dollar, an association official said.</p>
<p>The preliminary February data and revised January data were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		   Feb 97     yr/yr change	Jan 97 (revised)</p>
<p> Shipments     88,900	 -0.4 pct	 85,788  (+5.7 pct)</p>
<p>   Telecoms     3,700	 +4.4 pct	  3,776 (+15.4 pct)</p>
<p>   Elec Power  11,000	-16.7 pct	 11,381  (+2.9 pct)</p>
<p>   Electrical  22,900	 -4.3 pct	 22,788  (+1.7 pct)</p>
<p>   Automobile   6,500	 +7.1 pct	  5,645 (+17.9 pct)</p>
<p>   Constr'n    33,200	 +9.1 pct	 31,657 (+11.7 pct)</p>
<p>   Other	  6,900	 -7.9 pct	  7,044  (-0.8 pct)</p>
<p>   Exports	4,700	 +2.6 pct	  3,497 (-17.0 pct)</p>
<p> Orders	  88,300	 -5.7 pct	 84,720  (+5.6 pct)</p>
<p>   Exports	5,300	 +5.8 pct	  4,177 (-11.9 pct)</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
